## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates the ability to design multi-cloud Terraform architectures with per-tenant isolation, cross-cloud networking, and automated post-deployment validation including drift detection and reporting.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant Terraform Cloud workspaces with unique workspace keys
- Provider-agnostic networking module (AWS VPC, GCP VNet)
- Policy-as-code enforcement (OPA/Sentinel)
- Drift detection running after apply
- CI gates for tenant-scoped plans

## Code Example

```python
def detect_drift(desired_state, live_state):
    drift = {}
    for resource_id, desired_config in desired_state.items():
        live_config = live_state.get(resource_id)
        if not live_config:
            drift[resource_id] = "missing"
        elif live_config != desired_config:
            drift[resource_id] = {
                "expected": desired_config,
                "actual": live_config
            }
    return drift
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to structure a tiny Terraform project with proper state backends, a reusable module, and basic CI guards.

## Key Concepts
- Local vs remote backends and state isolation
- Modules and outputs for reusability
- State locking with DynamoDB
- CI gates that validate plan scope

## Code Example
```hcl
# backend for dev (local)
terraform {
  backend "local" {
    path = "terraform.tfstate"
  }
}
```

```hcl
# modules/storage/main.tf
resource "aws_s3_bucket" "bucket" {
  bucket = var.bucket_name
  acl    = "private"
  versioning {
    enabled = var.versioning
  }
}

resource "aws_dynamodb_table" "lock" {
  name           = "tfstate-lock"
  billing_mode   = "PAY_PER_REQUEST"
  hash_key       = "LockID"
  attribute {
    name = "LockID"
    type = "S"
  }
}

output "bucket_name" {
  value = aws_s3_bucket.bucket.bucket
}

output "locks_table_arn" {
  value = aws_dynamodb_table.lock.arn
}
```

```hcl
# modules/storage/variables.tf
variable "bucket_name" { type = string }
variable "versioning" { type = bool; default = true }
```

```hcl
# backend for prod (example)
terraform {
  backend "s3" {
    bucket         = "tfstate-prod"
    key            = "path/to/env/terraform.tfstate"
    region         = "us-east-1"
    dynamodb_table = "tfstate-lock"
  }
}
```

